    "attributes": {
        "input.value": "{\"messages\": [[{\"lc\": 1, \"type\": \"constructor\", \"id\": [\"langchain\", \"schema\", \"messages\", \"HumanMessage\"], \"kwargs\": {\"content\": \"You are evaluating whether a research summary accurately reflects its source material.\\n\\nQUERY: What is OpenTelemetry and what problem does it solve for distributed systems?\\n\\nSUMMARY TO EVALUATE:\\nOpenTelemetry is an open-source observability framework designed to provide standardized methods for collecting, processing, and exporting telemetry data such as metrics, logs, and traces from distributed systems. It addresses the challenge of monitoring complex, distributed architectures by offering a unified set of APIs, libraries, and agents that facilitate the collection of telemetry data across various services and platforms. This standardization helps developers and operators gain insights into system performance and behavior, enabling them to diagnose issues, optimize performance, and ensure reliability in distributed environments. OpenTelemetry supports a wide range of programming languages and integrates with numerous back-end systems, making it a versatile tool for observability in modern cloud-native applications.\\n\\nSOURCE EXCERPTS (ground truth):\\n[1] OpenTelemetry is an open-source observability framework that provides a standardized way to collect, process, and export telemetry data such as metrics, logs, and traces.\\n\\n[2] OpenTelemetry offers a developer-first control plane to manage logs, metrics, and traces, supporting OpenTelemetry, Prometheus, and over 100 integrations.\\n\\n[3] OpenTelemetry provides a unified set of APIs, libraries, and agents to collect telemetry data across various services and platforms, helping to monitor complex, distributed architectures.\\n\\nRate the faithfulness of the summary: what fraction of the factual claims in the\\nsummary are explicitly supported by at least one source excerpt above?\\n\\nReturn ONLY a JSON object \u2014 no markdown, no extra text:\\n{\\\"faithfulness\\\": <float 0.0-1.0>, \\\"label\\\": \\\"grounded\\\" or \\\"hallucinated\\\", \\\"reason\\\": \\\"<one sentence>\\\"}\\n\", \"type\": \"human\"}}]]}",
