        "input.value": "{\"messages\": [[{\"lc\": 1, \"type\": \"constructor\", \"id\": [\"langchain\", \"schema\", \"messages\", \"HumanMessage\"], \"kwargs\": {\"content\": \"You are evaluating whether a research summary accurately reflects its source material.\\n\\nQUERY: What is the OpenInference semantic convention and how does it extend OpenTelemetry for LLM applications?\\n\\nSUMMARY TO EVALUATE:\\nThe OpenInference semantic convention is designed to extend OpenTelemetry specifically for applications involving large language models (LLMs). It provides a set of conventions that enhance the tracing and monitoring capabilities of OpenTelemetry by addressing the unique requirements of LLM applications. This includes capturing specific metrics and traces that are relevant to the performance and behavior of LLMs, which are not typically covered by standard OpenTelemetry conventions. OpenInference aims to provide more granular insights into the operations of LLMs, facilitating better performance tuning and debugging in these complex systems.\\n\\nSOURCE EXCERPTS (ground truth):\\n[1] openinference_semantic_conventions - Rust... openinference-semantic-conventions 0.1.1... Dependencies opentelemetry ^0.31 normal... About docs.rs...\\n\\n[2] OpenInference vs. OpenTelemetry GenAI Conventions: Which Should You Use for Agent Tracing?... articleSection: Best Practices...\\n\\nRate the faithfulness of the summary: what fraction of the factual claims in the\\nsummary are explicitly supported by at least one source excerpt above?\\n\\nReturn ONLY a JSON object \u2014 no markdown, no extra text:\\n{\\\"faithfulness\\\": <float 0.0-1.0>, \\\"label\\\": \\\"grounded\\\" or \\\"hallucinated\\\", \\\"reason\\\": \\\"<one sentence>\\\"}\\n\", \"type\": \"human\"}}]]}",
