    "attributes": {
        "input.value": "{\"messages\": [[{\"lc\": 1, \"type\": \"constructor\", \"id\": [\"langchain\", \"schema\", \"messages\", \"HumanMessage\"], \"kwargs\": {\"content\": \"You are evaluating whether a research summary accurately reflects its source material.\\n\\nQUERY: What is the OpenInference semantic convention and how does it extend OpenTelemetry for LLM applications?\\n\\nSUMMARY TO EVALUATE:\\nThe OpenInference semantic convention is a framework designed to extend OpenTelemetry specifically for applications involving large language models (LLMs). It provides a set of conventions that enhance the tracing and monitoring capabilities of OpenTelemetry by addressing the unique requirements of LLM applications. This includes capturing detailed semantic information about the operations and interactions within these models, which is crucial for understanding and optimizing their performance. OpenInference aims to fill the gaps left by traditional telemetry systems when applied to the complex and dynamic nature of LLMs, offering more granular insights into their behavior and performance metrics.\\n\\nSOURCE EXCERPTS (ground truth):\\n[1] openinference_semantic_conventions - Rust... openinference-semantic-conventions 0.1.1... Dependencies opentelemetry ^0.31 normal... About docs.rs...\\n\\n[2] OpenInference vs. OpenTelemetry GenAI Conventions: Which Should You Use for Agent Tracing?... OpenInference aims to fill the gaps left by traditional telemetry systems when applied to the complex and dynamic nature of LLMs...\\n\\nRate the faithfulness of the summary: what fraction of the factual claims in the\\nsummary are explicitly supported by at least one source excerpt above?\\n\\nReturn ONLY a JSON object \u2014 no markdown, no extra text:\\n{\\\"faithfulness\\\": <float 0.0-1.0>, \\\"label\\\": \\\"grounded\\\" or \\\"hallucinated\\\", \\\"reason\\\": \\\"<one sentence>\\\"}\\n\", \"type\": \"human\"}}]]}",
