        "output.mime_type": "application/json",
        "llm.input_messages.0.message.role": "user",
        "llm.input_messages.0.message.content": "You are evaluating whether a research summary accurately reflects its source material.\n\nQUERY: How does Arize Phoenix compare to Langfuse for tracing LLM agent applications in 2025?\n\nSUMMARY TO EVALUATE:\nIn 2025, Arize Phoenix and Langfuse are both prominent tools for tracing LLM agent applications, but they have distinct features and strengths. Arize Phoenix is noted for its robust data visualization capabilities and ease of integration with existing machine learning workflows, making it a preferred choice for teams focused on detailed data analysis and model performance tracking. Langfuse, on the other hand, excels in providing comprehensive observability features specifically tailored for LLMs, including real-time monitoring and debugging tools that are highly valued by developers working on complex LLM applications. While both platforms offer valuable insights into LLM operations, the choice between them often depends on the specific needs of the development team, such as the importance of data visualization versus real-time monitoring capabilities.\n\nSOURCE EXCERPTS (ground truth):\n[1] Langfuse vs Phoenix Arize \u2014 LLM Observability Compared (2026) | MyEngineeringPath\n\n[2] Top 5 Leading Agent Observability Tools in 2025\n\nRate the faithfulness of the summary: what fraction of the factual claims in the\nsummary are explicitly supported by at least one source excerpt above?\n\nReturn ONLY a JSON object \u2014 no markdown, no extra text:\n{\"faithfulness\": <float 0.0-1.0>, \"label\": \"grounded\" or \"hallucinated\", \"reason\": \"<one sentence>\"}\n",
